.SH "NAME"
git-survey \- EXPERIMENTAL: Measure various repository dimensions of scale
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
(EXPERIMENTAL!) \fIgit survey\fR <options>
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Survey the repository and measure various dimensions of scale\&.
.sp
As repositories grow to "monorepo" size, certain data shapes can cause performance problems\&. \fBgit\-survey\fR attempts to measure and report on known problem areas\&.
.SS "Ref Selection and Reachable Objects"
.sp
In this first analysis phase, \fBgit\fR \fBsurvey\fR will iterate over the set of requested branches, tags, and other refs and treewalk over all of the reachable commits, trees, and blobs and generate various statistics\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-\-progress
.RS 4
Show progress\&. This is automatically enabled when interactive\&.
.RE
.SS "Ref Selection"
.sp
The following options control the set of refs that \fBgit\fR \fBsurvey\fR will examine\&. By default, \fBgit\fR \fBsurvey\fR will look at tags, local branches, and remote refs\&. If any of the following options are given, the default set is cleared and only refs for the given options are added\&.
.PP
\-\-all\-refs
.RS 4
Use all refs\&. This includes local branches, tags, remote refs, notes, and stashes\&. This option overrides all of the following\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-branches
.RS 4
Add local branches (\fBrefs/heads/\fR) to the set\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-tags
.RS 4
Add tags (\fBrefs/tags/\fR) to the set\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-remotes
.RS 4
Add remote branches (\fBrefs/remote/\fR) to the set\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-detached
.RS 4
Add HEAD to the set\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-other
.RS 4
Add notes (\fBrefs/notes/\fR) and stashes (\fBrefs/stash/\fR) to the set\&.
.RE
.SH "OUTPUT"
.sp
By default, \fBgit\fR \fBsurvey\fR will print information about the repository in a human\-readable format that includes overviews and tables\&.
.SS "References Summary"
.sp
The references summary includes a count of each kind of reference, including branches, remote refs, and tags (split by "all" and "annotated")\&.
.SS "Reachable Object Summary"
.sp
The reachable object summary shows the total number of each kind of Git object, including tags, commits, trees, and blobs\&.
.SH "GIT"
.sp
Part of the \fBgit\fR(1) suite
